# Friday — Mini Project: Dynamic Pages

[◀ Thursday: Client Components](./04-thursday-client-components.md) · [🏠 Index](./00-index.md)

## Goal

Build a small **App Router** project that ties the whole week together: dynamic routes, Server Component data fetching, `generateStaticParams`, and one interactive Client Component — a "like" button on each product page.

## Folder Structure

```
my-shop/
├── app/
│   ├── layout.js
│   ├── page.js
│   └── products/
│       └── [id]/
│           └── page.js
├── components/
│   └── LikeButton.js
├── lib/
│   └── products.js
└── package.json
```

## 1. Mock Data Source (`lib/products.js`)

```js
const products = [
  { id: "1", name: "Trail Running Shoes", price: 89, description: "Grippy, lightweight, built for mud." },
  { id: "2", name: "Insulated Water Bottle", price: 24, description: "Keeps drinks cold for 24 hours." },
  { id: "3", name: "Packable Rain Jacket", price: 59, description: "Folds into its own pocket." },
];

export async function getAllProducts() {
  return products;
}

export async function getProductById(id) {
  return products.find((p) => p.id === id);
}
```

## 2. Root Layout (`app/layout.js`)

```jsx
export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body style={{ fontFamily: "sans-serif", margin: 0, padding: "2rem" }}>
        {children}
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## 3. Home Page — List All Products (`app/page.js`)

```jsx
import Link from "next/link";
import { getAllProducts } from "../lib/products";

export default async function Home() {
  const products = await getAllProducts();

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Shop</h1>
      <ul>
        {products.map((p) => (
          <li key={p.id}>
            <Link href={`/products/${p.id}`}>{p.name}</Link> — ${p.price}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </main>
  );
}
```

## 4. Dynamic Product Page (`app/products/[id]/page.js`)

This Server Component fetches the product, pre-builds every product page via `generateStaticParams`, and embeds a small Client Component for the interactive part:

```jsx
import { getAllProducts, getProductById } from "../../../lib/products";
import LikeButton from "../../../components/LikeButton";

export async function generateStaticParams() {
  const products = await getAllProducts();
  return products.map((p) => ({ id: p.id }));
}

export default async function ProductPage({ params }) {
  const product = await getProductById(params.id);

  if (!product) {
    return <p>Product not found.</p>;
  }

  return (
    <article>
      <h1>{product.name}</h1>
      <p>${product.price}</p>
      <p>{product.description}</p>

      {/* Client Component — the only interactive piece on this page */}
      <LikeButton productId={product.id} />

      <p><a href="/">← Back to shop</a></p>
    </article>
  );
}
```

## 5. The One Client Component (`components/LikeButton.js`)

```jsx
"use client";

import { useState } from "react";

export default function LikeButton({ productId }) {
  const [liked, setLiked] = useState(false);

  return (
    <button onClick={() => setLiked((v) => !v)}>
      {liked ? "❤️ Liked" : "🤍 Like this"}
    </button>
  );
}
```

Notice the rest of `ProductPage` — the title, price, description — stays a **Server Component**. Only `LikeButton` ships JavaScript to the browser, because it's the only piece that actually needs `useState` and an `onClick` handler.

## 6. Run It

```bash
npm run dev
```

Visit `http://localhost:3000` — click into any product and press the like button. Everything except that button was rendered on the server.

## 7. Build for Production

```bash
npm run build
npm run start
```

Check the build output: each `/products/[id]` route should be listed as pre-rendered, confirming `generateStaticParams` did its job.

## Stretch Goals

- Add a `loading.js` in `app/products/[id]/` and artificially delay `getProductById` to see the loading state in action.
- Add a search/filter Client Component on the home page that doesn't require re-fetching from the server.
- Swap the mock data in `lib/products.js` for a real database call.
- Add `generateMetadata` to set a dynamic `<title>` per product.

